<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <!--
    Tauri merges this file into the bundled app's own Info.plist at package
    time (src-tauri/Info.plist is picked up by convention — there is no
    tauri.conf.json key pointing at it, which is exactly why this comment
    exists: deleting this file removes the behaviour below with nothing in the
    config to say it ever applied).

    LSUIElement makes this an "agent" application: no Dock icon, no entry in
    the app switcher, no application menu bar of its own. It lives in the
    status bar and nowhere else.

    This is the founder's brief, verbatim: "only menu bar would be cool — for
    example Ollama has an application but it's always on top of this menu bar
    even though application is closed."

    lib.rs ALSO sets ActivationPolicy::Accessory at startup, and the pair is
    not redundant. LSUIElement is read by the OS before any of this app's code
    runs, so there is not even a flash of a Dock icon at launch; the runtime
    policy is what keeps the behaviour true for a `cargo tauri dev` run and any
    other launch that does not go through the packaged bundle's Info.plist.

    The app still opens a real, focusable window for first-run sign-in. An
    LSUIElement app is allowed to — it just never claims a Dock tile for it.
  -->
  <key>LSUIElement</key>
  <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
